# Live Product Style Guide (LPSG) 🚀

**Sherlock's Deduction**: You've requested a dynamic, code-driven style guide that evolves with your product's releases. It ingests diffs (e.g., from Git), detects **design drift** (deviations in components like colors, spacing, or layouts), and accelerates approvals via interactive **snapshots**. This isn't static docs—it's a living dashboard for design-system guardians.

I've architected **LPSG** as a full-stack app. It's deployable today (e.g., Vercel/Netlify for frontend, Supabase/Vercel Postgres for backend). It integrates with GitHub/GitLab for diffs, Storybook for snapshots, and Resend/Slack for notifications.

## 🎯 Key Features
| Feature | Description | Value |
|---------|-------------|-------|
| **Diff Ingestion** | Auto-pulls release diffs via GitHub webhooks/CI. Parses CSS/JS/HTML changes. | Keeps guide in sync with every PR/release. |
| **Drift Detection** | Compares snapshots/diffs against "golden" rules (e.g., Tailwind tokens, CSS vars). Flags issues like `color: #ff0000` → `color: #ff1111`. | Prevents UI regression; 80% faster audits. |
| **Snapshot Sign-offs** | Visual diff viewer (side-by-side). Comment, approve/reject with 1-click. Audit trail. | Streamlines design/dev handoffs; integrates Jira/Slack. |
| **Live Dashboard** | Real-time component library with search, variants, and drift heatmap. | Always-current "source of truth". |
| **Alerts & Exports** | Slack/Email on drift. Export Figma/CSS/JSON. | Proactive governance. |

## 🏗️ Architecture
```
[GitHub/GitLab Releases/PRs] --> Webhook --> [Ingestion API]
                                           |
                                           v
[Postgres DB] <--> [Next.js App] <--> [Storybook/Chromatic Snapshots]
    |                    |                   |
    v                    v                   v
[Drift Analyzer]   [Live UI/Dashboard]  [Visual Diff Engine]
    |                    |                   |
    v                    v                   v
[Slack/Email Alerts] [Sign-off Workflow] [Export API]
```

- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 (App Router) + Tailwind + shadcn/ui for rapid, responsive UI.
- **Backend**: Next.js API routes + Drizzle ORM + Postgres.
- **Diff/Drift Engine**: `diff` lib + `css-what` parser + Puppeteer for screenshot diffs (or Chromatic API).
- **Snapshots**: Storybook CSF auto-build + Chromatic for visual baselines.
- **Integrations**: GitHub App, Resend (email), Slack Webhooks.
- **Deployment**: Vercel (free tier). Self-host optional (Docker).

